Let pkg-config link the MinGW zstd dynamically.

zstd-sys probes pkg-config with .statik(true). The pkg-config crate then
asks rustc for static=zstd whenever a libzstd.a sits in a directory that
is not a system root, and on Windows there are no system roots unless
PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR or SYSROOT is set. So the MinGW zstd's static
library is always taken and every binary carries its own copy of zstd.
Without the flag the import library is used and the binaries load
libzstd.dll.

msys2/MINGW-packages carries the same change as
zstd-sys-remove-statik.patch in twelve recipes, mingw-w64-dotslash among
them.

Upstream: not submitted from here
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -54,7 +54,6 @@
 
 fn pkg_config() -> (Vec<&'static str>, Vec<PathBuf>) {
     let library = pkg_config::Config::new()
-        .statik(true)
         .cargo_metadata(!cfg!(feature = "non-cargo"))
         .probe("libzstd")
         .expect("Can't probe for zstd in pkg-config");
